-- Rules of Court 2021 (Singapore), G.N. No. S 914/2021, current version as at 5 November 2026.
-- ORDER 23: CONTEMPT OF COURT (rules 1 to 18), layer 1 (the law, objectively).
-- Source: a plain-text rendering made by a converter script from Singapore Statutes Online.
-- It is not the official text, and nothing here has been checked against the official text.
--
-- HOW TO READ A RESULT.  A function answers `MAYBE BOOLEAN` unless its name says it returns something else.
--   JUST TRUE    the text says yes on these facts.
--   JUST FALSE   the text says no in its own words: a definition that "means", a condition introduced by
--                "if", "where" or "only", a flat negative ("Nothing in ... is taken as affecting"), or a
--                period fixed in the text's own words and missed (ruling of 2026-11-05).
--   NOTHING      the text does not answer: it is silent on what follows a failure to comply with a "must",
--                the list is not closed, a term or a rule lies outside the sources, or a grant ("may") is
--                limited by its own wording and the case is outside the limit.
-- A caller must never turn NOTHING into FALSE.
-- Every requirement here is subject to the Court's discretion to order otherwise (O 3 r 2(1)); no function
-- threads that as an input.
-- A period is counted by Order 3, Rule 3 (roc1's range); each function takes the last day that Rule gives
-- as the input `o 3 r 3 the last day for doing the act`.  The Interpretation Act does not apply to the
-- calculation of time in these Rules (O 3 r 3(1)), so it is not used here.

