§§ `Rule 1 -- Definitions of this Order`
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- "unless the context otherwise requires" is not threaded (PLAN.md section 7, item 9).

-- src:3559 | 1. In this Order, unless the context otherwise requires — “Act” means the Administration of Justice (Protection) Act 2016;
@ref O 23 r 1 "Act" (src:3559)
GIVEN `the enactment is the Administration of Justice (Protection) Act 2016` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 23 r 1 "Act" is the Administration of Justice (Protection) Act 2016` MEANS
    IF `the enactment is the Administration of Justice (Protection) Act 2016`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“Act” means the Administration of Justice (Protection) Act 2016"

-- src:3560 | “committal applicant” means the person who is applying for or has obtained a committal order against the committal respondent;
@ref O 23 r 1 "committal applicant" (src:3560)
GIVEN `the person is applying for a committal order against the committal respondent` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person has obtained a committal order against the committal respondent` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 23 r 1 "committal applicant" is the person applying for or having obtained a committal order` MEANS
    IF `the person is applying for a committal order against the committal respondent` OR `the person has obtained a committal order against the committal respondent`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“committal applicant” means the person who is applying for or has obtained a committal order against the committal respondent"

-- src:3561 | “committal respondent” means the person against whom a committal order is sought or made;
@ref O 23 r 1 "committal respondent" (src:3561)
GIVEN `a committal order is sought against the person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a committal order has been made against the person` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 23 r 1 "committal respondent" is the person against whom a committal order is sought or made` MEANS
    IF `a committal order is sought against the person` OR `a committal order has been made against the person`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“committal respondent” means the person against whom a committal order is sought or made"

DECLARE `o 23 r 1 "contempt of court" kind of contempt` IS ONE OF
    `o 23 r 1 "contempt of court" contempt under the Act`
    `o 23 r 1 "contempt of court" contempt under the common law`
    `o 23 r 1 "contempt of court" any other contempt`

-- src:3562 | “contempt of court” means contempt of court under the Act and includes, subject to section 8, contempt of court under the common law;
@ref O 23 r 1 "contempt of court" (src:3562)
GIVEN kind IS A `o 23 r 1 "contempt of court" kind of contempt`
      `section 8 of the Act allows contempt under the common law` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 23 r 1 "contempt of court" is contempt under the Act, and includes contempt under the common law` MEANS
    CONSIDER kind
    WHEN `o 23 r 1 "contempt of court" contempt under the Act` THEN JUST TRUE -- the first limb: "means contempt of court under the Act"
    WHEN `o 23 r 1 "contempt of court" contempt under the common law` THEN
        CONSIDER `section 8 of the Act allows contempt under the common law`
        WHEN JUST allowed THEN
            IF allowed
            THEN JUST TRUE -- the second limb: "includes, subject to section 8, contempt of court under the common law"
            ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "subject to section 8" cuts the inclusion back, and what section 8 says is outside the sources
        WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): section 8 of the Administration of Justice (Protection) Act 2016 is not among the sources
    WHEN `o 23 r 1 "contempt of court" any other contempt` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "means ... and includes", so the Rule does not close the list

-- src:3563 | “non‑publication direction” means a direction under section 13;
@ref O 23 r 1 "non-publication direction" (src:3563)
GIVEN `the direction is a direction under section 13 of the Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 23 r 1 "non-publication direction" is a direction under section 13` MEANS
    IF `the direction is a direction under section 13 of the Act`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“non‑publication direction” means a direction under section 13"

-- src:3564 | “section” means a section of the Act.
@ref O 23 r 1 "section" (src:3564)
GIVEN `the provision is a section of the Administration of Justice (Protection) Act 2016` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 23 r 1 "section" is a section of the Act` MEANS
    IF `the provision is a section of the Administration of Justice (Protection) Act 2016`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“section” means a section of the Act"

