§§ `Rule 2 -- Committal order for contempt of court`
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- src:3566 | 2. The power of the Court to punish for contempt of court may be exercised by a committal order.
@ref O 23 r 2 (src:3566)
GIVEN `the punishment is by a committal order` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 23 r 2 the power to punish for contempt of court may be exercised by a committal order` MEANS
    IF `the punishment is by a committal order`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the Rule names a committal order as one way of exercising the power and does not say it is the only way

