§§ `Rule 3 -- Application for permission of Court`
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- src:3568 | 3. —(1) A committal applicant must first apply to the Court for permission to make an application for a committal order. (2) An application for permission must be made by originating application without notice or by summons without notice in an action (as the case may be) to a Judge.
@ref O 23 r 3(1) (src:3568)
GIVEN `the person is a committal applicant` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person applied to the Court for permission before applying for the committal order` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 23 r 3(1) the committal applicant has first applied to the Court for permission` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF (NOT `the person is a committal applicant`) THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the duty is a committal applicant's
        IF `the person applied to the Court for permission before applying for the committal order` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the Rule says a committal applicant "must first apply" and does not say what follows if the person did not

DECLARE `o 23 r 3(2) how the application for permission is made` IS ONE OF
    `o 23 r 3(2) by originating application without notice`
    `o 23 r 3(2) by summons without notice in an action`
    `o 23 r 3(2) in some other way`

@ref O 23 r 3(2) (src:3568)
GIVEN how IS A `o 23 r 3(2) how the application for permission is made`
      `the application arises in an action already begun` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the application is made to a Judge` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 23 r 3(2) the application for permission is made in the way required` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF (NOT `the application is made to a Judge`) THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): "to a Judge" is a requirement, and the Rule does not say what follows if it is not met
        IF how EQUALS `o 23 r 3(2) by originating application without notice` AND (NOT `the application arises in an action already begun`) THEN JUST TRUE -- "originating application without notice ... (as the case may be)": no action
        IF how EQUALS `o 23 r 3(2) by summons without notice in an action` AND `the application arises in an action already begun` THEN JUST TRUE -- "summons without notice in an action (as the case may be)": an action
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the Rule says how the application "must be made" and does not say what follows if it is made another way

-- src:3569 | (3) The application must be supported by an affidavit setting out — ( a )
-- src:3570 | the committal applicant’s name, description and address;
-- src:3571 | ( b )
-- src:3572 | the committal respondent’s name, description and address; and
-- src:3573 | ( c )
-- src:3574 | the grounds on which the committal order is sought.
@ref O 23 r 3(3) (src:3569-3574)
GIVEN `the application is supported by an affidavit` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the affidavit sets out the committal applicant's name, description and address` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the affidavit sets out the committal respondent's name, description and address` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the affidavit sets out the grounds on which the committal order is sought` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 23 r 3(3) the affidavit supporting the application sets out what is required` MEANS
    IF    `the application is supported by an affidavit`
      AND `the affidavit sets out the committal applicant's name, description and address` -- (a)
      AND `the affidavit sets out the committal respondent's name, description and address` -- (b)
      AND `the affidavit sets out the grounds on which the committal order is sought` -- (c)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the Rule says what the affidavit must set out and does not say what follows if it does not

