§§ `Rule 4 -- Application for committal order after permission of Court granted`
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- src:3576 | 4. —(1) After permission is granted under Rule 3, the committal applicant must apply for the committal order within 14 days by summons in the originating application without notice or by summons in the action, and serve the following on the committal respondent by personal service: ( a )
-- src:3577 | the originating application without notice or summons without notice for permission under Rule 3(2);
-- src:3578 | ( b )
-- src:3579 | the supporting affidavit under Rule 3(3);
-- src:3580 | ( c )
-- src:3581 | the order granting permission under Rule 3(1);
-- src:3582 | ( d )
-- src:3583 | the summons for the committal order under this paragraph.
@ref O 23 r 4(1) (src:3576-3583)
`o 23 r 4(1) the period for applying for the committal order` MEANS Period WITH
    `period length` IS 14
    `period unit` IS Days
    `period direction` IS `After the anchor`

DECLARE `o 23 r 4(1) how the committal order is applied for` IS ONE OF
    `o 23 r 4(1) by summons in the originating application without notice`
    `o 23 r 4(1) by summons in the action`
    `o 23 r 4(1) in some other way`

@ref O 23 r 4(1) (src:3576-3583)
GIVEN `permission has been granted under Rule 3` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date the application for the committal order was made` IS A DATE
      `o 3 r 3 the last day for doing the act` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 23 r 4(1) the application for the committal order is made within 14 days after permission` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF (NOT `permission has been granted under Rule 3`) THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words, ruling of 2026-11-05 (b), "After" read as "where": assumed, see F-ASSUMED): "After permission is granted under Rule 3"
        IF `the date the application for the committal order was made` AT MOST `o 3 r 3 the last day for doing the act` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words, ruling of 2026-11-05 (a)): "within 14 days"

@ref O 23 r 4(1) (src:3576-3583)
GIVEN how IS A `o 23 r 4(1) how the committal order is applied for`
      `the application arises in an action already begun` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 23 r 4(1) the application for the committal order is made in the way required` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF how EQUALS `o 23 r 4(1) by summons in the originating application without notice` AND (NOT `the application arises in an action already begun`) THEN JUST TRUE
        IF how EQUALS `o 23 r 4(1) by summons in the action` AND `the application arises in an action already begun` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the Rule says how the application must be made and does not say what follows if it is made another way

@ref O 23 r 4(1) (src:3576-3583)
GIVEN `the committal respondent was served by personal service` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the originating application without notice or summons without notice for permission was served` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the supporting affidavit under Rule 3(3) was served` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the order granting permission under Rule 3(1) was served` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the summons for the committal order was served` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 23 r 4(1) the four documents have been served on the committal respondent by personal service` MEANS
    IF    `the committal respondent was served by personal service`
      AND `the originating application without notice or summons without notice for permission was served` -- (a)
      AND `the supporting affidavit under Rule 3(3) was served` -- (b)
      AND `the order granting permission under Rule 3(1) was served` -- (c)
      AND `the summons for the committal order was served` -- (d)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the Rule gives no time for the service (the 14 days attach to the application: fork F-O23-1) and does not say what follows if it is not done

-- src:3584 | (2) There must be at least 21 days between the service under paragraph (1) and the hearing date.
@ref O 23 r 4(2) (src:3584)
`o 23 r 4(2) the minimum gap between service and the hearing` MEANS Period WITH
    `period length` IS 21
    `period unit` IS Days
    `period direction` IS `Before the anchor`

@ref O 23 r 4(2) (src:3584)
GIVEN `the date of the service under paragraph (1)` IS A DATE
      `o 3 r 3 the last day for doing the act` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 23 r 4(2) there are at least 21 days between the service and the hearing date` MEANS
    IF `the date of the service under paragraph (1)` AT MOST `o 3 r 3 the last day for doing the act`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words, ruling of 2026-11-05 (a)): "at least 21 days between the service under paragraph (1) and the hearing date"

