§§ `Rule 5 -- Power to commit without application`
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- src:3586 | 5. —(1) Where by virtue of any written law, the General Division has power to punish or take steps for the punishment of any person charged with having done anything in relation to a court, tribunal or person which would, if it had been done in relation to the General Division, have been a contempt of that Court, a committal order may be made by the General Division. (2) Nothing in Rules 2, 3 and 4 is taken as affecting the power of the General Division, the Appellate Division or the Court of Appeal to make a committal order on its own accord against a person guilty of contempt of court.
@ref O 23 r 5(1) (src:3586)
GIVEN `by virtue of a written law the General Division has power to punish or take steps for the punishment of the person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the thing done in relation to a court, tribunal or person would have been a contempt of the General Division if done in relation to it` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 23 r 5(1) a committal order may be made by the General Division` MEANS
    IF    `by virtue of a written law the General Division has power to punish or take steps for the punishment of the person`
      AND `the thing done in relation to a court, tribunal or person would have been a contempt of the General Division if done in relation to it`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words, ruling of 2026-11-05 (b)): "Where by virtue of any written law, the General Division has power to punish ..."

@ref O 23 r 5(2) (src:3586)
GIVEN court IS A `Court level`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 23 r 5(2) Rules 2, 3 and 4 affect the power to make a committal order on its own accord` MEANS
    CONSIDER court
    WHEN `General Division` THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Nothing in Rules 2, 3 and 4 is taken as affecting the power of the General Division"
    WHEN `Appellate Division` THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Nothing in Rules 2, 3 and 4 is taken as affecting the power of ... the Appellate Division"
    WHEN `Court of Appeal` THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Nothing in Rules 2, 3 and 4 is taken as affecting the power of ... the Court of Appeal"
    WHEN `District Court` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the paragraph names three courts only
    WHEN `Magistrate's Court` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the paragraph names three courts only
    WHEN `Singapore International Commercial Court` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the paragraph names three courts only
    WHEN `Family Division` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the paragraph names three courts only

