§§ `Rule 6 -- Transfer to General Division`
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- src:3588 | 6. —(1) An application under section 10(4) to transfer a case in a State Court to the General Division must be made to a Judge sitting in the General Division by originating application. (2) In hearing such an application, the General Division may order the case sought to be transferred and any related proceedings to be stayed until after the final determination of the application.
@ref O 23 r 6(1) (src:3588)
GIVEN `the application is under section 10(4) to transfer a case in a State Court to the General Division` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the application is made to a Judge sitting in the General Division` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the application is made by originating application` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 23 r 6(1) the application to transfer a case is made in the way required` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF (NOT `the application is under section 10(4) to transfer a case in a State Court to the General Division`) THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the paragraph speaks only of an application under section 10(4)
        IF `the application is made to a Judge sitting in the General Division` AND `the application is made by originating application` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the Rule says how the application "must be made" and does not say what follows if it is made another way

@ref O 23 r 6(2) (src:3588)
GIVEN `the General Division is hearing an application under paragraph (1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the order is to stay the case sought to be transferred and any related proceedings until after the final determination of the application` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 23 r 6(2) the General Division may order the case and related proceedings stayed` MEANS
    IF `the General Division is hearing an application under paragraph (1)` AND `the order is to stay the case sought to be transferred and any related proceedings until after the final determination of the application`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "In hearing such an application, the General Division may order ..." names one kind of order

DECLARE `o 23 r 6(3)(a) what the General Division may do on ordering a transfer` IS ONE OF
    `o 23 r 6(3)(a)(i) set aside or affirm an order made by the State Court`
    `o 23 r 6(3)(a)(ii) modify Rules 3 and 4 in their application to the case`
    `o 23 r 6(3)(a)(iii) make any other order relating to the transfer`
    `o 23 r 6(3)(a) something else`

