        IF what EQUALS `o 23 r 6(3)(a)(i) set aside or affirm an order made by the State Court` THEN JUST TRUE
        IF what EQUALS `o 23 r 6(3)(a)(ii) modify Rules 3 and 4 in their application to the case` THEN JUST TRUE
        IF what EQUALS `o 23 r 6(3)(a)(iii) make any other order relating to the transfer` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "the General Division may —" lists three things

-- src:3596 | ( b )
-- src:3597 | the Registrar of the State Courts must send to the Registrar of the Supreme Court the file of the proceedings, all documents, exhibits and a certified copy of the notes of evidence (if any) of the proceedings; and
@ref O 23 r 6(3)(b) (src:3596-3597)
GIVEN `the General Division has ordered the case in a State Court to be transferred under section 10(4)` IS A BOOLEAN
