§§ `Rule 7 -- Provisions as to hearing`
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- src:3601 | 7. —(1) The Court must hear in open court an application for a committal order or an application under section 10(4) to transfer a case to the General Division, but may hear the application in private in the following cases: ( a )
-- src:3602 | where the application arises out of proceedings relating to the wardship or adoption of an infant or wholly or mainly to the guardianship, custody, maintenance or upbringing of an infant, or rights of access to an infant;
-- src:3603 | ( b )
-- src:3604 | where the application arises out of proceedings relating to a person who lacks capacity within the meaning of the Mental Capacity Act in relation to matters concerning his or her property and affairs;
-- src:3605 | ( c )
-- src:3606 | where the application is made in the General Division and arises out of proceedings in a Small Claims Tribunal or an Employment Claims Tribunal constituted under section 4 of the State Courts Act;
-- src:3607 | ( d )
-- src:3608 | where the application arises out of proceedings in which a secret process, discovery or invention was in issue;
-- src:3609 | ( e )
-- src:3610 | where it appears to the Court that, in the interests of the administration of justice or for reasons of national security, the application should be heard in private.
@ref O 23 r 7(1) (src:3601-3610)
GIVEN `it is an application for a committal order or an application under section 10(4) to transfer a case to the General Division` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the application arises out of proceedings relating to wardship or adoption of an infant, or wholly or mainly to guardianship, custody, maintenance or upbringing of an infant, or rights of access to an infant` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the application arises out of proceedings relating to a person who lacks capacity within the meaning of the Mental Capacity Act in relation to matters concerning property and affairs` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the application is made in the General Division and arises out of proceedings in a Small Claims Tribunal or an Employment Claims Tribunal constituted under section 4 of the State Courts Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the application arises out of proceedings in which a secret process, discovery or invention was in issue` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it appears to the Court that, in the interests of the administration of justice or for reasons of national security, the application should be heard in private` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 23 r 7(1) the Court may hear the application in private` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF (NOT `it is an application for a committal order or an application under section 10(4) to transfer a case to the General Division`) THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the paragraph speaks of those two applications
        IF `the application arises out of proceedings relating to wardship or adoption of an infant, or wholly or mainly to guardianship, custody, maintenance or upbringing of an infant, or rights of access to an infant` THEN JUST TRUE -- (a)
        IF `the application arises out of proceedings relating to a person who lacks capacity within the meaning of the Mental Capacity Act in relation to matters concerning property and affairs` THEN JUST TRUE -- (b)
        IF `the application is made in the General Division and arises out of proceedings in a Small Claims Tribunal or an Employment Claims Tribunal constituted under section 4 of the State Courts Act` THEN JUST TRUE -- (c)
        IF `the application arises out of proceedings in which a secret process, discovery or invention was in issue` THEN JUST TRUE -- (d)
        IF `it appears to the Court that, in the interests of the administration of justice or for reasons of national security, the application should be heard in private` THEN JUST TRUE -- (e)
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words, ruling of 2026-11-05 (b)): each of cases (a) to (e) begins "where", so outside them the Court may not hear the application in private (fork F-O23-2: the other reading is that the list is not closed, which would answer NOTHING)

@ref O 23 r 7(1) (src:3601-3610)
GIVEN `it is an application for a committal order or an application under section 10(4) to transfer a case to the General Division` IS A BOOLEAN
      `one of cases (a) to (e) applies` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 23 r 7(1) the Court must hear the application in open court` MEANS
    -- The exception is the one the "but" gives: the Court "must hear in open court ... but may hear the application in private in the
    -- following cases".  This function takes the one fact the exception turns on, whether one of cases (a) to (e) applies, and agrees with
    -- `o 23 r 7(1) the Court may hear the application in private` on every row (F-O23-2): outside the cases private is JUST FALSE and open
    -- court JUST TRUE; inside them private is JUST TRUE and open court JUST FALSE.  The tests assert the pairs side by side.
    BRANCH
        IF (NOT `it is an application for a committal order or an application under section 10(4) to transfer a case to the General Division`) THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the paragraph speaks of those two applications
        IF (NOT `one of cases (a) to (e) applies`) THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "but may hear the application in private in the following cases": inside them the open-court duty gives way

-- src:3611 | (2) If the Court hears the application in private under paragraph (1) and decides to make a committal order against the committal respondent, it must state in open court — ( a )
-- src:3612 | the name of the committal respondent;
-- src:3613 | ( b )
-- src:3614 | in general terms the nature of the contempt of court in respect of which the committal order is being made; and
-- src:3615 | ( c )
-- src:3616 | if the committal respondent is being committed for a fixed period, the length of that period.
@ref O 23 r 7(2) (src:3611-3616)
GIVEN `the Court hears the application in private under paragraph (1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Court decides to make a committal order against the committal respondent` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 23 r 7(2) the Court must state in open court what the paragraph lists` MEANS
    IF `the Court hears the application in private under paragraph (1)` AND `the Court decides to make a committal order against the committal respondent`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If the Court hears the application in private under paragraph (1) and decides to make a committal order ..., it must state in open court"

@ref O 23 r 7(2) (src:3611-3616)
GIVEN `the Court stated the name of the committal respondent` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Court stated in general terms the nature of the contempt of court in respect of which the committal order is being made` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the committal respondent is being committed for a fixed period` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Court stated the length of that period` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 23 r 7(2) the Court has stated in open court what the paragraph lists` MEANS
    IF    `the Court stated the name of the committal respondent` -- (a)
      AND `the Court stated in general terms the nature of the contempt of court in respect of which the committal order is being made` -- (b)
      AND ((NOT `the committal respondent is being committed for a fixed period`) OR `the Court stated the length of that period`) -- (c)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the paragraph says what the Court "must state" and does not say what follows if it does not

-- src:3617 | (3) The committal applicant must rely on only the grounds set out in the affidavit under Rule 3(3).
@ref O 23 r 7(3) (src:3617)
GIVEN `the ground is set out in the affidavit under Rule 3(3)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 23 r 7(3) the committal applicant may rely on the ground` MEANS
    IF `the ground is set out in the affidavit under Rule 3(3)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must rely on only the grounds set out in the affidavit under Rule 3(3)"

-- src:3618 | (4) At the hearing of the application for a committal order, the committal respondent — ( a )
-- src:3619 | must rely on the matters stated in his or her affidavit, if any; but
@ref O 23 r 7(4)(a) (src:3618-3619)
GIVEN `the committal respondent has an affidavit` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 23 r 7(4)(a) the committal respondent must rely on the matters stated in the affidavit` MEANS
    IF `the committal respondent has an affidavit`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words, "if" rule): "must rely on the matters stated in his or her affidavit, if any": with no affidavit there is nothing to rely on under this sub-paragraph"

-- src:3620 | ( b )
-- src:3621 | may, with the permission of the Court, give oral evidence on his or her own behalf.
@ref O 23 r 7(4)(b) (src:3620-3621)
GIVEN `the Court gave permission` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the evidence is given on the committal respondent's own behalf` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 23 r 7(4)(b) the committal respondent may give oral evidence` MEANS
    IF `the Court gave permission` AND `the evidence is given on the committal respondent's own behalf`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "may, with the permission of the Court, give oral evidence on his or her own behalf"

DECLARE `o 23 r 7(5) matter for a live link order for the committal respondent` IS ONE OF
    `o 23 r 7(5)(a)(i) the ability of the committal respondent to effectively conduct the defence`
    `o 23 r 7(5)(a)(ii) the ability of an advocate representing the committal respondent to effectively conduct the defence`
    `o 23 r 7(5)(b) the ability of the committal applicant to effectively conduct the proceedings`
    `o 23 r 7(5)(c) the ability of the committal respondent to consult and instruct an advocate in private`
    `o 23 r 7(5)(d)(i) technical measures to verify the identities of persons giving evidence or appearing`
    `o 23 r 7(5)(d)(ii) technical measures to prevent the committal respondent being coached or coerced`
    `o 23 r 7(5)(d)(iii) technical measures to prevent the proceedings being recorded`
    `o 23 r 7(5)(d)(iv) technical measures to control and restrict who can access or observe the proceedings`
    `o 23 r 7(5)(e) the likelihood that the Court may require the committal respondent to handle physical evidence`
    `o 23 r 7(5)(f) whether a judgment or order requiring the committal respondent to be taken into custody may be delivered or made during the proceedings`
    `o 23 r 7(5) some other matter`

-- src:3622 | (5) For the purposes of section 26A(9), in making any order allowing a committal respondent to give evidence or to appear (other than to give evidence) by means of a live video or live television link under section 26A(1), the Court is to have regard to the following matters: ( a )
-- src:3623 | whether the order would affect the ability of any of the following persons to effectively conduct the defence of the committal respondent: (i)
-- src:3624 | the committal respondent;
-- src:3625 | (ii)
-- src:3626 | an advocate representing the committal respondent;
-- src:3627 | ( b )
-- src:3628 | whether the order would affect the ability of the committal applicant to effectively conduct those proceedings;
-- src:3629 | ( c )
-- src:3630 | whether the order would affect the ability of the committal respondent to consult and instruct his or her advocate in private;
-- src:3631 | ( d )
-- src:3632 | whether adequate technical measures are available to the Court — (i)
-- src:3633 | to verify the identities of persons giving evidence or appearing by means of the live video or live television link;
-- src:3634 | (ii)
-- src:3635 | to prevent the committal respondent from being coached or coerced while giving evidence or appearing by means of a live video or live television link;
-- src:3636 | (iii)
-- src:3637 | to prevent the proceedings from being recorded; and
-- src:3638 | (iv)
-- src:3639 | to control and restrict the persons who are able to access or observe the proceedings;
-- src:3640 | ( e )
-- src:3641 | the likelihood that the Court may require the committal respondent to handle any physical evidence;
-- src:3642 | ( f )
-- src:3643 | whether a judgment or order requiring the committal respondent to be taken into custody may be delivered or made during the proceedings. [S 206/2022 wef 01/04/2022]
@ref O 23 r 7(5) (src:3622-3643)
GIVEN `the order allows the committal respondent to give evidence or to appear by live video or live television link under section 26A(1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      matter IS A `o 23 r 7(5) matter for a live link order for the committal respondent`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 23 r 7(5) the Court is to have regard to the matter` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF (NOT `the order allows the committal respondent to give evidence or to appear by live video or live television link under section 26A(1)`) THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the paragraph speaks of an order under section 26A(1)
        IF matter EQUALS `o 23 r 7(5) some other matter` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): "to have regard to the following matters" does not say "only"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE -- each of (a)(i) to (f)

DECLARE `o 23 r 7(6) matter for a live link order for a witness` IS ONE OF
    `o 23 r 7(6)(a)(i) the ability of the committal respondent to effectively conduct the defence`
    `o 23 r 7(6)(a)(ii) the ability of an advocate representing the committal respondent to effectively conduct the defence`
    `o 23 r 7(6)(b) the ability of the committal applicant to effectively conduct the proceedings`
    `o 23 r 7(6)(c)(i) technical measures to verify the identities of persons giving evidence`
    `o 23 r 7(6)(c)(ii) technical measures to prevent the witness being coached or coerced`
    `o 23 r 7(6)(c)(iii) technical measures to prevent the proceedings being recorded`
    `o 23 r 7(6)(c)(iv) technical measures to control and restrict who can access or observe the proceedings`
    `o 23 r 7(6)(d) the likelihood that the Court may require the witness to handle physical evidence`
    `o 23 r 7(6)(e) the reason why an expert witness is not giving evidence from Singapore`
    `o 23 r 7(6) some other matter`

-- src:3644 | (6) For the purposes of section 26A(9), in making any order allowing a witness (not being the committal respondent) to give evidence by means of a live video or live television link under section 26A(2) or (3), the Court is to have regard to the following matters: ( a )
-- src:3645 | whether the order would affect the ability of any of the following persons to effectively conduct the defence of the committal respondent: (i)
-- src:3646 | the committal respondent;
-- src:3647 | (ii)
-- src:3648 | an advocate representing the committal respondent;
-- src:3649 | ( b )
-- src:3650 | whether the order would affect the ability of the committal applicant to effectively conduct those proceedings;
-- src:3651 | ( c )
-- src:3652 | whether adequate technical measures are available to the Court — (i)
-- src:3653 | to verify the identities of persons giving evidence by means of the live video or live television link;
-- src:3654 | (ii)
-- src:3655 | to prevent the witness from being coached or coerced while giving evidence by means of a live video or live television link;
-- src:3656 | (iii)
-- src:3657 | to prevent the proceedings from being recorded; and
-- src:3658 | (iv)
-- src:3659 | to control and restrict the persons who are able to access or observe the proceedings;
-- src:3660 | ( d )
-- src:3661 | the likelihood that the Court may require the witness to handle any physical evidence;
-- src:3662 | ( e )
-- src:3663 | in the case of an order under section 26A(3) allowing an expert witness to give evidence from a place that is not in Singapore — the reason why the expert witness is not giving evidence from Singapore. [S 206/2022 wef 01/04/2022]
@ref O 23 r 7(6) (src:3644-3663)
GIVEN `the order allows a witness who is not the committal respondent to give evidence by live video or live television link under section 26A(2) or (3)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the order is under section 26A(3) and allows an expert witness to give evidence from a place not in Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN
      matter IS A `o 23 r 7(6) matter for a live link order for a witness`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 23 r 7(6) the Court is to have regard to the matter` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF (NOT `the order allows a witness who is not the committal respondent to give evidence by live video or live television link under section 26A(2) or (3)`) THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the paragraph speaks of an order under section 26A(2) or (3)
        IF matter EQUALS `o 23 r 7(6) some other matter` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): "to have regard to the following matters" does not say "only"
        IF matter EQUALS `o 23 r 7(6)(e) the reason why an expert witness is not giving evidence from Singapore` THEN
            IF `the order is under section 26A(3) and allows an expert witness to give evidence from a place not in Singapore`
            THEN JUST TRUE -- (e): "in the case of an order under section 26A(3) allowing an expert witness ..."
            ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): (e) is for an order under section 26A(3) allowing an expert witness to give evidence from outside Singapore
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE -- each of (a)(i) to (d)

