§§ `Rule 8 -- Power to suspend execution of committal order`
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- src:3665 | 8. —(1) The Court may order the execution of the committal order to be suspended for such period or on such terms or conditions as it may specify. (2) Where the Court makes an order under paragraph (1), the committal applicant must serve a notice on the committal respondent informing the committal respondent of the terms of that order.
@ref O 23 r 8(1) (src:3665)
GIVEN `a committal order has been made` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 23 r 8(1) the Court may order the execution of the committal order to be suspended` MEANS
    IF `a committal order has been made`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the power is over "the committal order"

@ref O 23 r 8(2) (src:3665)
GIVEN `the Court has made an order under paragraph (1)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 23 r 8(2) the committal applicant must serve a notice of the terms of the order` MEANS
    IF `the Court has made an order under paragraph (1)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words, ruling of 2026-11-05 (b)): "Where the Court makes an order under paragraph (1)"

@ref O 23 r 8(2) (src:3665)
GIVEN `the committal applicant served a notice on the committal respondent` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the notice informs the committal respondent of the terms of the order` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 23 r 8(2) the committal applicant has served the notice required` MEANS
    IF `the committal applicant served a notice on the committal respondent` AND `the notice informs the committal respondent of the terms of the order`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the paragraph says the committal applicant "must serve a notice" and does not say what follows if not

