    IF `the application is made by summons` AND `the summons is supported by an affidavit` AND `the summons is served on the committal respondent`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the paragraph says what the application "must be" and does not say what follows if it is not

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
§§ `Rule 9 -- Discharge of committal respondent`
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- src:3669 | 9. —(1) Where a committal respondent has been committed for contempt of court, the Court may discharge him or her upon his or her application. (2) Where a committal respondent has been committed for contempt of court under section 4 in relation to his or her failure to deliver any thing to some other person or to deposit it in Court or elsewhere, then, if the thing is in the possession or control of the committal respondent, the Sheriff may take possession of it as if it were the property of the committal respondent and, without limiting paragraph (1), the Court may discharge the committal respondent and give directions for dealing with the thing.
@ref O 23 r 9(1) (src:3669)
GIVEN `the committal respondent has been committed for contempt of court` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the committal respondent applies to be discharged` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 23 r 9(1) the Court may discharge the committal respondent` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF (NOT `the committal respondent has been committed for contempt of court`) THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words, ruling of 2026-11-05 (b)): "Where a committal respondent has been committed for contempt of court"
        IF `the committal respondent applies to be discharged` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words, ruling of 2026-11-05 (b), "upon" read as "where"): "the Court may discharge him or her upon his or her application"

@ref O 23 r 9(2) (src:3669)
GIVEN `the committal respondent has been committed under section 4 for failing to deliver a thing to another person or to deposit it in Court or elsewhere` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the thing is in the possession or control of the committal respondent` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 23 r 9(2) the Sheriff may take possession of the thing` MEANS
    IF    `the committal respondent has been committed under section 4 for failing to deliver a thing to another person or to deposit it in Court or elsewhere`
      AND `the thing is in the possession or control of the committal respondent`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where a committal respondent has been committed ... under section 4 ..., then, if the thing is in the possession or control of the committal respondent, the Sheriff may take possession of it"

@ref O 23 r 9(2) (src:3669)
GIVEN `the committal respondent has been committed under section 4 for failing to deliver a thing to another person or to deposit it in Court or elsewhere` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the thing is in the possession or control of the committal respondent` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 23 r 9(2) the Court may discharge the committal respondent and give directions for dealing with the thing` MEANS
    IF    `the committal respondent has been committed under section 4 for failing to deliver a thing to another person or to deposit it in Court or elsewhere`
      AND `the thing is in the possession or control of the committal respondent`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where ... then, if the thing is in the possession or control of the committal respondent, ... the Court may discharge the committal respondent and give directions"

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
§§ `Rule 10 -- Saving for other powers`
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

DECLARE `o 23 r 10 an order the Court has power to make` IS ONE OF
    `o 23 r 10 an order requiring a person punishable by virtue of a written law as if guilty of contempt of court to pay a fine`
    `o 23 r 10 an order requiring such a person to give security for good behaviour`
    `o 23 r 10 any other order`

-- src:3671 | 10. Nothing in Rules 1 to 9 is to be taken as affecting the power of the Court to make an order requiring a person punishable by virtue of any written law in like manner as if he or she had been guilty of contempt of court, to pay a fine or to give security for his or her good behaviour, and those Rules, so far as applicable and with the necessary modifications, apply in relation to an application for such an order as they apply in relation to an application for a committal order.
@ref O 23 r 10 (src:3671)
GIVEN order IS A `o 23 r 10 an order the Court has power to make`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 23 r 10 Rules 1 to 9 affect the Court's power to make the order` MEANS
    CONSIDER order
    WHEN `o 23 r 10 an order requiring a person punishable by virtue of a written law as if guilty of contempt of court to pay a fine` THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Nothing in Rules 1 to 9 is to be taken as affecting the power of the Court to make an order requiring a person ... to pay a fine"
    WHEN `o 23 r 10 an order requiring such a person to give security for good behaviour` THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Nothing in Rules 1 to 9 is to be taken as affecting the power of the Court to make an order ... to give security for his or her good behaviour"
    WHEN `o 23 r 10 any other order` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the saving is for the two orders it names

@ref O 23 r 10 (src:3671)
GIVEN `it is an application for an order to pay a fine or give security for good behaviour made against a person punishable by virtue of a written law as if guilty of contempt of court` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Rule is applicable to the application, with the necessary modifications` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 23 r 10 Rules 1 to 9 apply to the application as they apply to an application for a committal order` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF (NOT `it is an application for an order to pay a fine or give security for good behaviour made against a person punishable by virtue of a written law as if guilty of contempt of court`) THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the sentence speaks of "an application for such an order"
        IF `the Rule is applicable to the application, with the necessary modifications` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "so far as applicable and with the necessary modifications"

