§§ `Rule 11 -- Form of committal order`
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- src:3673 | 11. —(1) A committal order must be in Form 42. (2) The committal applicant must serve on the Sheriff’s office by filing a copy of — ( a )
@ref O 23 r 11(1) (src:3673)
`o 23 r 11(1) the form of the committal order` MEANS "Form 42"

@ref O 23 r 11(1) (src:3673)
GIVEN `the form the committal order is in` IS A STRING
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 23 r 11(1) the committal order is in the form required` MEANS
    IF `the form the committal order is in` EQUALS `o 23 r 11(1) the form of the committal order`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the paragraph says the order "must be in Form 42" and does not say what follows if it is not

-- src:3673 | 11. —(1) A committal order must be in Form 42. (2) The committal applicant must serve on the Sheriff’s office by filing a copy of — ( a )
-- src:3674 | the committal order; and
-- src:3675 | ( b )
-- src:3676 | a written undertaking by the solicitor for the committal applicant (if the committal applicant is represented by a solicitor) or by the committal applicant (if the committal applicant is not represented by a solicitor) to — (i)
-- src:3677 | pay upon request all charges, expenses and fees incurred by or payable to the Sheriff and the Singapore Police Force in complying with the committal order; and
-- src:3678 | (ii)
-- src:3679 | indemnify the Sheriff and the Singapore Police Force against all claims, costs and expenses arising from complying with the committal order.
@ref O 23 r 11(2) (src:3673-3679)
GIVEN `the committal applicant is represented by a solicitor` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a copy of the committal order was filed to serve it on the Sheriff's office` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a written undertaking was filed with it` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the undertaking is by the solicitor for the committal applicant` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the undertaking is by the committal applicant` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the undertaking is to pay upon request all charges, expenses and fees incurred by or payable to the Sheriff and the Singapore Police Force in complying with the committal order` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the undertaking is to indemnify the Sheriff and the Singapore Police Force against all claims, costs and expenses arising from complying with the committal order` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 23 r 11(2) the committal applicant has served on the Sheriff's office what is required` MEANS
    IF    `a copy of the committal order was filed to serve it on the Sheriff's office` -- (a)
      AND `a written undertaking was filed with it`
      AND (   (`the committal applicant is represented by a solicitor` AND `the undertaking is by the solicitor for the committal applicant`)
           OR ((NOT `the committal applicant is represented by a solicitor`) AND `the undertaking is by the committal applicant`)) -- (b)
      AND `the undertaking is to pay upon request all charges, expenses and fees incurred by or payable to the Sheriff and the Singapore Police Force in complying with the committal order` -- (b)(i)
      AND `the undertaking is to indemnify the Sheriff and the Singapore Police Force against all claims, costs and expenses arising from complying with the committal order` -- (b)(ii)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the paragraph says what the committal applicant "must serve" and does not say what follows if not

-- src:3680 | (3) The committal applicant must also deposit the amount of money requested by the Sheriff before the Sheriff complies with the committal order and from time to time.
-- src:3681 | Committal proceedings before Employment Claims Tribunals (O. 23, r. 12)
@ref O 23 r 11(3) (src:3680-3681)
GIVEN `the committal applicant deposited the amount of money the Sheriff requested before the Sheriff complied with the committal order` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the committal applicant deposited each further amount the Sheriff requested from time to time` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 23 r 11(3) the committal applicant has deposited the money requested by the Sheriff` MEANS
    IF `the committal applicant deposited the amount of money the Sheriff requested before the Sheriff complied with the committal order` AND `the committal applicant deposited each further amount the Sheriff requested from time to time`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the paragraph says the committal applicant "must also deposit" and does not say what follows if not

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
§§ `Rules 12 to 14 -- Committal proceedings before tribunals`
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- Rules 12, 13 and 14 each apply Rules 1 to 11 "(except Rule 7(1) and (2))" to a different tribunal.  The
-- helper below answers for a rule and a paragraph (0 where the rule has no paragraph, or the whole rule is meant);
-- keyed by numbers because the core has no type for a reference to a rule (NEEDS-CORE.md).
-- src:3682 | 12. —(1) Rules 1 to 11 (except Rule 7(1) and (2)) apply to committal proceedings before a tribunal. (2) For the purposes of applying this Order to committal proceedings before a tribunal, unless the context otherwise requires — ( a )
@ref O 23 r 12(1) (src:3682)
GIVEN rule IS A NUMBER
      paragraph IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 23 r 12(1) Rules 1 to 11 apply to committal proceedings before a tribunal` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF rule EQUALS 7 AND (paragraph EQUALS 1 OR paragraph EQUALS 2) THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(except Rule 7(1) and (2))"
        IF rule AT LEAST 1 AND rule AT MOST 11 THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the paragraph speaks of "Rules 1 to 11"

DECLARE `o 23 r 12(2) a reference` IS ONE OF
    `o 23 r 12(2) a reference to a Court`
    `o 23 r 12(2) a reference to a Judge`
    `o 23 r 12(2) a reference to something else`

DECLARE `o 23 r 12(2) how the reference is read` IS ONE OF
    `o 23 r 12(2) a tribunal or a tribunal magistrate`
    `o 23 r 12(2) a tribunal magistrate`
    `o 23 r 12(2) not changed by this paragraph`

-- src:3682 | 12. —(1) Rules 1 to 11 (except Rule 7(1) and (2)) apply to committal proceedings before a tribunal. (2) For the purposes of applying this Order to committal proceedings before a tribunal, unless the context otherwise requires — ( a )
-- src:3683 | any reference to a Court is a reference to a tribunal or a tribunal magistrate; and
-- src:3684 | ( b )
-- src:3685 | any reference to a Judge is a reference to a tribunal magistrate.
@ref O 23 r 12(2) (src:3682-3685)
GIVEN reference IS A `o 23 r 12(2) a reference`
GIVETH A `o 23 r 12(2) how the reference is read`
`o 23 r 12(2) how a reference in Order 23 is read for a committal proceeding before an Employment Claims Tribunal` MEANS
    CONSIDER reference
    WHEN `o 23 r 12(2) a reference to a Court` THEN `o 23 r 12(2) a tribunal or a tribunal magistrate` -- (a), unless the context otherwise requires
    WHEN `o 23 r 12(2) a reference to a Judge` THEN `o 23 r 12(2) a tribunal magistrate` -- (b), unless the context otherwise requires
    WHEN `o 23 r 12(2) a reference to something else` THEN `o 23 r 12(2) not changed by this paragraph` -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): paragraph (2) names references to a Court and to a Judge

-- src:3686 | (3) The court fees that apply to proceedings under this Order in a District Court apply to proceedings under this Order in a tribunal.
-- src:3687 | (4) The hearing fees prescribed in the Employment Claims Rules 2017 (G.N. No. S 104/2017) apply to the hearing of any proceedings under this Order in a tribunal.
@ref O 23 r 12(3) and (4) (src:3686-3687)
GIVEN `the proceedings are under Order 23 in a tribunal` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE `Court level`
`o 23 r 12(3) the court fees that apply to proceedings under this Order in a tribunal are those in` MEANS
    IF `the proceedings are under Order 23 in a tribunal`
    THEN JUST `District Court` -- "The court fees that apply to proceedings under this Order in a District Court apply to proceedings under this Order in a tribunal"
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the paragraph speaks of proceedings in a tribunal

@ref O 23 r 12(4) (src:3687)
`o 23 r 12(4) the instrument that prescribes the hearing fees in a tribunal` MEANS "Employment Claims Rules 2017 (G.N. No. S 104/2017)"

-- src:3688 | (5) In this Rule — “tribunal” means a State Court called an Employment Claims Tribunal constituted under section 4 of the State Courts Act;
-- src:3689 | “tribunal magistrate” has the meaning given by section 2(1) of the Employment Claims Act 2016.
@ref O 23 r 12(5) (src:3688-3689)
GIVEN `it is a State Court called an Employment Claims Tribunal` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is constituted under section 4 of the State Courts Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 23 r 12(5) "tribunal" is a State Court called an Employment Claims Tribunal constituted under section 4 of the State Courts Act` MEANS
    IF `it is a State Court called an Employment Claims Tribunal` AND `it is constituted under section 4 of the State Courts Act`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“tribunal” means a State Court called an Employment Claims Tribunal constituted under section 4 of the State Courts Act"

@ref O 23 r 12(5) (src:3689)
GIVEN `employment claims act 2016 s 2(1) the person is a tribunal magistrate` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 23 r 12(5) "tribunal magistrate" has the meaning given by section 2(1) of the Employment Claims Act 2016` MEANS
    `employment claims act 2016 s 2(1) the person is a tribunal magistrate` -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text) when absent: section 2(1) of the Employment Claims Act 2016 is not among the sources

