-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
§§ `Rule 15 -- Application by Attorney-General for permission to give non-publication direction`
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- src:3707 | 15. —(1) An application by the Attorney‑General for permission to give a non‑publication direction must be made by originating application without notice supported by an affidavit. (2) The supporting affidavit may be made by a person authorised by the Attorney‑General.
@ref O 23 r 15(1) and (2) (src:3707)
GIVEN `the application is by the Attorney-General for permission to give a non-publication direction` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the application is made by originating application without notice` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the application is supported by an affidavit` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the affidavit is made by the Attorney-General or by a person authorised by the Attorney-General` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 23 r 15(1) the Attorney-General's application is made in the way required` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF (NOT `the application is by the Attorney-General for permission to give a non-publication direction`) THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the paragraph speaks of an application by the Attorney-General
        IF `the application is made by originating application without notice` AND `the application is supported by an affidavit` AND `the affidavit is made by the Attorney-General or by a person authorised by the Attorney-General` THEN JUST TRUE -- (1) and (2): "The supporting affidavit may be made by a person authorised by the Attorney‑General"
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the paragraph says how the application "must be made" and does not say what follows if it is made another way

-- src:3708 | (3) The supporting affidavit must — ( a )
-- src:3709 | have annexed to it a copy of the proposed non‑publication direction;
-- src:3710 | ( b )
-- src:3711 | state the grounds for believing that there is a prima facie case that — (i)
-- src:3712 | the person to whom the proposed non‑publication direction will apply has published the matter that is the subject of the proposed non‑publication direction; and
-- src:3713 | (ii)
-- src:3714 | the publication of the matter that is the subject of the non‑publication direction would satisfy section 13(7)( b )(i), (ii) or (iii);
-- src:3715 | ( c )
-- src:3716 | state the reasons for any exception or condition in the proposed non‑publication direction; and
-- src:3717 | ( d )
-- src:3718 | state that the Attorney‑General is satisfied that it is in the public interest to give the proposed non‑publication direction.
@ref O 23 r 15(3) (src:3708-3718)
GIVEN `a copy of the proposed non-publication direction is annexed` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the affidavit states the grounds for believing there is a prima facie case that the person to whom the proposed direction will apply has published the matter` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the affidavit states the grounds for believing there is a prima facie case that the publication would satisfy section 13(7)(b)(i), (ii) or (iii)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the affidavit states the reasons for any exception or condition in the proposed direction` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the affidavit states that the Attorney-General is satisfied that it is in the public interest to give the proposed direction` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 23 r 15(3) the supporting affidavit states what it must` MEANS
    IF    `a copy of the proposed non-publication direction is annexed` -- (a)
      AND `the affidavit states the grounds for believing there is a prima facie case that the person to whom the proposed direction will apply has published the matter` -- (b)(i)
      AND `the affidavit states the grounds for believing there is a prima facie case that the publication would satisfy section 13(7)(b)(i), (ii) or (iii)` -- (b)(ii)
      AND `the affidavit states the reasons for any exception or condition in the proposed direction` -- (c)
      AND `the affidavit states that the Attorney-General is satisfied that it is in the public interest to give the proposed direction` -- (d)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the paragraph says what the affidavit "must" do and does not say what follows if it does not

-- src:3719 | (4) The Court’s permission to give a non‑publication direction lapses if the direction is not served in accordance with the Act within 14 days after the day on which permission is granted.
@ref O 23 r 15(4) (src:3719)
`o 23 r 15(4) the period for serving the non-publication direction` MEANS Period WITH
    `period length` IS 14
    `period unit` IS Days
    `period direction` IS `After the anchor`

@ref O 23 r 15(4) (src:3719)
GIVEN `the date the direction was served in accordance with the Act` IS A MAYBE DATE
      `o 3 r 3 the last day for doing the act` IS A DATE
      `the date it is asked about` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 23 r 15(4) the Court's permission to give the non-publication direction lapses` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the date the direction was served in accordance with the Act`
    WHEN JUST served THEN
        IF served AT MOST `o 3 r 3 the last day for doing the act`
        THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words, ruling of 2026-11-05 (a)): "lapses if the direction is not served in accordance with the Act within 14 days"
        ELSE JUST TRUE -- "lapses if the direction is not served ... within 14 days after the day on which permission is granted"
    WHEN NOTHING THEN
        IF `the date it is asked about` GREATER THAN `o 3 r 3 the last day for doing the act`
        THEN JUST TRUE -- the direction has not been served and the 14 days have run
        ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): the permission lapses "if the direction is not served ... within 14 days", and the 14 days have not run

-- src:3720 | (5) After a non‑publication direction is served, a person authorised by the Attorney‑General must file an affidavit stating that the direction has been served in accordance with the Act and giving particulars of the service.
@ref O 23 r 15(5) (src:3720)
GIVEN `the direction has been served` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a person authorised by the Attorney-General filed an affidavit` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the affidavit states that the direction has been served in accordance with the Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the affidavit gives particulars of the service` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 23 r 15(5) the affidavit of service of the non-publication direction has been filed` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF (NOT `the direction has been served`) THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words, ruling of 2026-11-05 (b)): "After a non‑publication direction is served"
        IF `a person authorised by the Attorney-General filed an affidavit` AND `the affidavit states that the direction has been served in accordance with the Act` AND `the affidavit gives particulars of the service` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the paragraph says what the person "must file" and does not say what follows if not

@ref O 23 r 15(5) (src:3720)
`o 23 r 15(5) the person who must file the affidavit of service of the non-publication direction` MEANS "a person authorised by the Attorney-General"
