`o 23 r 16(9) the date from which the order setting aside the direction takes effect` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the other date the Court specified in the order`
    WHEN JUST specified THEN specified -- "or such other date as the Court may specify in the order"
    WHEN NOTHING THEN `the date of the order of Court setting aside the direction` -- "takes effect from the date of the order"

-- src:3733 | (10) An order of Court to vary a non‑publication direction takes effect — ( a )
-- src:3734 | insofar as the direction and the variation apply to the applicant — from the date of the order or such other date as the Court may specify in the order; and
-- src:3735 | ( b )
-- src:3736 | insofar as the direction and the variation apply to a person other than the applicant — from the date on which the order is served on the person or such later date as the Court may specify in the order.
@ref O 23 r 16(10)(a) (src:3733-3736)
GIVEN `the date of the order of Court varying the direction` IS A DATE
      `the other date the Court specified in the order` IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`o 23 r 16(10)(a) the date from which the order varying the direction takes effect as to the applicant` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the other date the Court specified in the order`
    WHEN JUST specified THEN specified -- "or such other date as the Court may specify in the order"
    WHEN NOTHING THEN `the date of the order of Court varying the direction` -- "from the date of the order"

@ref O 23 r 16(10)(b) (src:3735-3736)
GIVEN `the date the order was served on the person` IS A DATE
      `the later date the Court specified in the order` IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`o 23 r 16(10)(b) the date from which the order varying the direction takes effect as to a person other than the applicant` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the later date the Court specified in the order`
    WHEN JUST specified THEN
        IF specified GREATER THAN `the date the order was served on the person`
        THEN JUST specified -- "or such later date as the Court may specify in the order"
        ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): a date that is not later than the date of service is not "such later date", and the paragraph says nothing of it
    WHEN NOTHING THEN JUST `the date the order was served on the person` -- "from the date on which the order is served on the person"

-- The function above returns a date, so it cannot answer JUST FALSE for a date that is not later than the date of service; this is its yes/no twin (F-ASSUMED).
@ref O 23 r 16(10)(b) (src:3735-3736)
GIVEN `the date the order was served on the person` IS A DATE
      `the date the Court specified in the order` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 23 r 16(10)(b) the date the Court specified is a later date than the date of service` MEANS
    IF `the date the Court specified in the order` GREATER THAN `the date the order was served on the person`
    THEN JUST TRUE -- "such later date as the Court may specify in the order"
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words, ruling of 2026-11-05 (a)): "such later date as the Court may specify in the order": a date that is not later than the date of service is outside what the paragraph allows

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
§§ `Rule 17 -- Order to arrest committal respondent`
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- src:3738 | 17. —(1) The Court may order the Sheriff or any police officer to arrest and bring before the Court, as soon as is practicable, a committal respondent who fails to attend any proceedings in Court or who disobeys any order of the Court. (2) The Court may include in the order to arrest under paragraph (1) conditions relating to the giving of security by the committal respondent or to any other matter.
@ref O 23 r 17(1) (src:3738)
GIVEN `the committal respondent failed to attend a proceeding in Court` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the committal respondent disobeyed an order of the Court` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 23 r 17(1) the Court may order the Sheriff or a police officer to arrest and bring the committal respondent before the Court` MEANS
    IF `the committal respondent failed to attend a proceeding in Court` OR `the committal respondent disobeyed an order of the Court`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "who fails to attend any proceedings in Court or who disobeys any order of the Court"

@ref O 23 r 17(2) (src:3738)
GIVEN `an order to arrest has been made under paragraph (1)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 23 r 17(2) the Court may include conditions about security or any other matter in the order to arrest` MEANS
    IF `an order to arrest has been made under paragraph (1)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the power is over "the order to arrest under paragraph (1)"

-- src:3739 | (3) A letter from the Registrar stating the Court’s order made under paragraph (1) is sufficient authority for the Sheriff or any police officer to effect the arrest.
@ref O 23 r 17(3) (src:3739)
GIVEN `the letter is from the Registrar` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the letter states the Court's order made under paragraph (1)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 23 r 17(3) the letter is sufficient authority for the Sheriff or a police officer to effect the arrest` MEANS
    IF `the letter is from the Registrar` AND `the letter states the Court's order made under paragraph (1)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A letter from the Registrar stating the Court’s order made under paragraph (1)"

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
§§ `Rule 18 -- Sheriff may engage auxiliary police officer or other security agency`
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- src:3741 | 18. —(1) The Sheriff may engage, or direct the applicant to engage, any auxiliary police officer appointed under the Police Force Act or other security agency to assist him or her in the discharge of his or her duties under this Order. (2) Any amount of money incurred by the Sheriff under paragraph (1) is considered as part of the charges, expenses and fees incurred in complying with a committal order.
@ref O 23 r 18(1) (src:3741)
GIVEN `the person is an auxiliary police officer appointed under the Police Force Act, or a security agency` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the engagement is to assist the Sheriff in the discharge of the Sheriff's duties under this Order` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 23 r 18(1) the Sheriff may engage, or direct the applicant to engage, the person` MEANS
    IF `the person is an auxiliary police officer appointed under the Police Force Act, or a security agency` AND `the engagement is to assist the Sheriff in the discharge of the Sheriff's duties under this Order`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "any auxiliary police officer appointed under the Police Force Act or other security agency to assist him or her in the discharge of his or her duties under this Order"

@ref O 23 r 18(2) (src:3741)
GIVEN `the amount was incurred by the Sheriff under paragraph (1)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 23 r 18(2) the amount is part of the charges, expenses and fees incurred in complying with a committal order` MEANS
    IF `the amount was incurred by the Sheriff under paragraph (1)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the paragraph speaks of "Any amount of money incurred by the Sheriff under paragraph (1)"

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
§§ `The duties of Order 23 as regulative rules`
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- Each rule below says the same thing as the decision function named in its comment; the decision function is
-- the one the tests assert, because a #TRACE prints a result and counts as no assertion on this binary.  The
-- days are the days of the Rules' own count (O 3 r 3).  The Hohfeld kind of each is recorded in NOTES.md.

DECLARE `o 23 party` IS ONE OF
    `o 23 the committal applicant`
    `o 23 the applicant to vary or set aside a non-publication direction`

DECLARE `o 23 act` IS ONE OF
    `o 23 r 4(1) apply for the committal order`
    `o 23 r 7(3) rely on a ground not set out in the affidavit`
    `o 23 r 8(2) serve a notice of the terms of the suspension`
    `o 23 r 11(3) deposit the money the Sheriff requested`
    `o 23 r 16(7) serve the order setting aside or varying the direction`

-- src:3576 | 4. —(1) After permission is granted under Rule 3, the committal applicant must apply for the committal order within 14 days by summons in the originating application without notice or by summons in the action, and serve the following on the committal respondent by personal service: ( a )
-- src:3577 | the originating application without notice or summons without notice for permission under Rule 3(2);
-- src:3578 | ( b )
-- src:3579 | the supporting affidavit under Rule 3(3);
-- src:3580 | ( c )
-- src:3581 | the order granting permission under Rule 3(1);
-- src:3582 | ( d )
-- src:3583 | the summons for the committal order under this paragraph.
@ref O 23 r 4(1) (src:3576-3583)
GIVETH A DEONTIC `o 23 party` `o 23 act`
`o 23 r 4(1) the committal applicant must apply for the committal order within 14 days` MEANS
    PARTY `o 23 the committal applicant`
    MUST `o 23 r 4(1) apply for the committal order`
    WITHIN 14
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BECAUSE "the committal applicant did not apply for the committal order within 14 days after permission was granted"

-- src:3617 | (3) The committal applicant must rely on only the grounds set out in the affidavit under Rule 3(3).
@ref O 23 r 7(3) (src:3617)
GIVETH A DEONTIC `o 23 party` `o 23 act`
`o 23 r 7(3) the committal applicant shall not rely on a ground not set out in the affidavit` MEANS
    PARTY `o 23 the committal applicant`
    SHANT `o 23 r 7(3) rely on a ground not set out in the affidavit`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BECAUSE "the committal applicant relied on a ground that is not set out in the affidavit under Rule 3(3)"

-- src:3665 | 8. —(1) The Court may order the execution of the committal order to be suspended for such period or on such terms or conditions as it may specify. (2) Where the Court makes an order under paragraph (1), the committal applicant must serve a notice on the committal respondent informing the committal respondent of the terms of that order.
@ref O 23 r 8(2) (src:3665)
GIVETH A DEONTIC `o 23 party` `o 23 act`
`o 23 r 8(2) the committal applicant must serve a notice of the terms of the suspension` MEANS
    PARTY `o 23 the committal applicant`
    MUST `o 23 r 8(2) serve a notice of the terms of the suspension`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BECAUSE "the committal applicant did not serve a notice of the terms of the suspension on the committal respondent"

-- src:3680 | (3) The committal applicant must also deposit the amount of money requested by the Sheriff before the Sheriff complies with the committal order and from time to time.
-- src:3681 | Committal proceedings before Employment Claims Tribunals (O. 23, r. 12)
@ref O 23 r 11(3) (src:3680-3681)
GIVETH A DEONTIC `o 23 party` `o 23 act`
`o 23 r 11(3) the committal applicant must deposit the money the Sheriff requested` MEANS
    PARTY `o 23 the committal applicant`
    MUST `o 23 r 11(3) deposit the money the Sheriff requested`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BECAUSE "the committal applicant did not deposit the amount the Sheriff requested"

-- src:3727 | (7) If the Court sets aside or varies a non‑publication direction, the applicant must serve the order of the Court within 14 days after the date of the order of the Court — ( a )
-- src:3728 | on the person to whom the direction applies (unless the person is the applicant); and
-- src:3729 | ( b )
-- src:3730 | any other person whom the Court orders to be served.
@ref O 23 r 16(7) (src:3727-3730)
GIVETH A DEONTIC `o 23 party` `o 23 act`
`o 23 r 16(7) the applicant must serve the order within 14 days after the date of the order` MEANS
    PARTY `o 23 the applicant to vary or set aside a non-publication direction`
    MUST `o 23 r 16(7) serve the order setting aside or varying the direction`
    WITHIN 14
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BECAUSE "the applicant did not serve the order within 14 days after the date of the order"
